The BLE bridge (`src/ble_bridge.*`), the Nordic UART wire protocol used to talk to the
Claude Desktop "Hardware Buddy" developer-mode feature, the AnimatedGIF-based character
rendering path, and the `tools/prep_character.py` art pipeline originate from that project
and retain its MIT license and copyright notice (see LICENSE).

Everything else in this repository — the T-Display-S3 board shim, the landscape UI, the
screen state machine, the usage daemon, and the pixel art — is new code written for this
project.

---

Inspiration, not code: this project's idle/usage screen is inspired by the *idea* of
Clawdmeter (https://github.com/HermannBjorgvin/Clawdmeter) — a menu-bar app that shows
Claude usage and quota reset countdowns. Clawdmeter ships with no LICENSE file, which makes
it all-rights-reserved by default, so no source from that project was read, copied, or
consulted while writing `daemon/`. The daemon's method for computing usage (polling
`api.anthropic.com/v1/messages` and reading the `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-*` response
headers) was derived independently from Anthropic's own API behavior, not from Clawdmeter's
implementation.

No artwork, pixel art, or "Clawd" character assets from Clawdmeter are used anywhere in this
repository. The sprites in `art/` are original.
